function COMPONENT(request : dval) {
    var page := dval({source_page: ""})
    page["source_page"] = "type/request"
    page["kind"] = "type"
    page["slug"] = "request"
    page["route"] = "/doc/type/request/"
    page["title"] = "Request snapshot"
    page["content"] = "Every Capy handler receives one parameter, `request`, of type `dval`. It is a snapshot of the request taken when the handler is entered — reading it never touches the network, and reading the same field twice always gives the same answer.\n\nRead scalars through a converter with a fallback, so a key that is absent has a defined value rather than an error:\n\n    var name := string(request.query.name, \"guest\")\n    var page := s64(request.query.page, 1)\n    var debug := bool(request.query.debug, false)\n\nTest for presence with the `?` suffix, which is `true` when the key exists:\n\n    if request.query.token? { print(\"token supplied\\n\") }\n\n## Fields\n\n| Field | Type | Contains |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `method` | string | `GET`, `POST`, and so on |\n| `query` | map | parsed query-string parameters |\n| `form` | map | parsed form body parameters |\n| `params` | map | merged query and form parameters. Form values win when keys match. |\n| `body` | string | the raw request body |\n| `headers` | map | request headers, lowercased with dashes: `content-type`, `x-request-id` |\n| `cookies` | map | request cookies by name |\n| `files` | array | uploaded files, each with `name`, `size`, `temporary_path` |\n| `route` | map | `path`, `page`, `raw_path`, `valid` |\n| `url` | map | `script`, `base` |\n| `server` | map | remaining server and CGI variables, original uppercase names |\n| `session` | map | the current session snapshot |\n| `props` | map | properties passed by a component caller |\n| `config` | map | request-visible configuration |\n| `connection` | map | connection information |\n| `unit` | string | the source path of the unit currently executing |\n| `websocket` | map | `connection_id`, `scope`, `opcode`, `binary`, `connections` |\n| `call` | map | dispatch information for the current call |\n| `ou"
    page["content"] = string(page["content"], "") + "t` | map | mutable response state: `status`, `header`, `cookie`, and `buffer` |\n\n## Headers and server variables\n\n`headers` holds anything that arrived as an HTTP header, renamed for readability: the transport's `HTTP_X_REQUEST_ID` appears as `request.headers[\"x-request-id\"]`. `content-type` and `content-length` are included even though they arrive without the `HTTP_` prefix. Use bracket syntax for these, since the names contain dashes.\n\n`server` holds everything else — `QUERY_STRING`, `REMOTE_ADDR`, `SERVER_NAME` — under the original uppercase names. `method`, `route`, and `url` are lifted out of `server` into their own fields, so look for them there rather than in `server`.\n\n## Reading and writing\n\nThe snapshot is read-only except for `out`. Set `request.out.status`, `request.out.header`, `request.out.cookie`, or `request.out.buffer` to change the response. `print()` appends to the response body.\n\nA component receives the caller's `props` for the duration of the call. Bearer restores the previous value after the call. When nested components write back the same field, the outer component write-back wins.\n"
    page["label"] = "request"
    page["capy_sig_lines"] = dval(["handler request : dval"])
    page["param_lines"] = dval([])
    page["notes"] = dval([])
    page["warnings"] = dval([])
    page["see"] = dval([{label: "render", href: "/doc/handler/render/"}, {label: "component", href: "/doc/handler/component/"}, {label: "cli", href: "/doc/handler/cli/"}, {label: "ws", href: "/doc/handler/ws/"}, {label: "string", href: "/doc/api/string/"}])
    page["examples"] = dval([{entry: "render", caption: "", body: "print(string(request.query.name, \"guest\"), \"\\n\")\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "branch on the method and read a form field", body: "if string(request.method, \"\") == \"POST\" {\n    print(\"saved \", string(request.form.answer, \"\"), \"\\n\")\n} else {\n    print(\"<form method=\\\"post\\\"><input name=\\\"answer\\\"></form>\", \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "read a header and a cookie", body: "print(string(request.headers[\"user-agent\"], \"unknown\"), \"\\n\")\nprint(string(request.cookies.session, \"none\"), \"\\n\")\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "list uploaded files", body: "for file := request.files {\n    print(string(file.name, \"\"), \" \", u64(file.size, 0), \"\\n\")\n}\n"}, {entry: "render", caption: "check presence before use", body: "if request.query.page? {\n    print(\"page \", s64(request.query.page, 1), \"\\n\")\n} else {\n    print(\"no page requested\\n\")\n}\n"}])
    page["guide_examples"] = dval([])
    component_render("/doc/components/doc_page.capy", page)
}
